+# Bun migration
+
+Requires Bun 1.4.4 or newer. Validated with the supplied Bun 1.4.4 executable;
+no global runtime installation was changed. There were no original package
+ dependencies or test suites. Added exact `@types/bun` 1.4.4 for checking;
+`bun.lock` pins it and its transitive declaration dependencies.
+
+## Commands
+
+- `bun install --frozen-lockfile`
+- `bun run run <operation> [path] [text]`
+- `bun run typecheck` (strict checking of both entry points and regression tests)
+- `bun run check` (retained check task alias)
+- `bun run test` (five added regression tests, no skips)
+
+Operations remain `new`, `replace`, `read`, `missing`, `list`, and `child`.
+No serve or build task existed. Deno configuration and execution were removed.
+Formatting and linting remain outside this migration's scope.
+
+## Behavior
+
+Node filesystem promises preserve exclusive creation (`wx`), default replacement
+and truncation, and awaited file closure. TextDecoder preserves the original
+UTF-8 BOM removal and malformed-byte replacement behavior. Directory listings
+sort regular filenames and exclude directories and symbolic links. Only ENOENT
+becomes `{ "missing": true }`; other filesystem errors still fail the command.
+
+The child uses the current Bun executable and a filesystem path derived from its
+module URL. Both pipes drain concurrently, preserving all 120,001 bytes per pipe
+and the child exit code 7 in the parent JSON response. The parent still exits
+successfully after reporting this child result. Runtime stack traces and native
+filesystem error wording differ from Deno, while command success/failure and JSON
+outputs are preserved.
+
+## Security and environment
+
+Bun has the host process's filesystem, environment, subprocess, and network
+access. It does not reproduce Deno's permission sandbox. The previous launcher
+allowed all reads, writes, and subprocess execution but did not grant network or
+environment access; those runtime restrictions are now absent. Use an external
+OS/container policy if those restrictions are required. No additional application
+network requests or environment reads were introduced.
+
+`bunfig.toml` disables implicit dotenv loading, matching the original explicit
+environment behavior. Run commands from the project directory so this config is
+loaded. No dependency lifecycle script trust was enabled.
+
+## Validation
+
+Before editing, Deno strict checking and filesystem/CLI/subprocess behavior checks
+passed. After migration, strict checking passes and five regression tests pass
+with zero failures/skips. Tests cover exclusive creation, truncation, Unicode and
+BOM/malformed-byte decoding, missing/error classification, sorted directory
+filtering, and large dual-stream child output.
+
+A fresh temporary copy installed successfully with the frozen lockfile and no
+project node_modules, then passed typecheck, check, and test with Deno absent from
+PATH. Additional checks exercised package-script argument forwarding, unknown
+operation failure, preservation on exclusive-create failure, full child output,
+and dotenv suppression through the script runner. An injected type error in a
+temporary copy of child.ts correctly failed typecheck, confirming whole-project
+coverage. No deployment or hosted environment was tested.
